NNAAMMEE
     eeddiittlliinnee — line editing user interface

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     When a program using the editline(3) library prompts for an input string
     using the function el_wgets(3), it reads characters from the terminal.
     Invalid input bytes that do not form characters are silently discarded.
     For each character read, one editor command is executed.  The mapping of
     input characters to editor commands depends on the editing mode.  There
     are three editing modes:  vi insert mode, vi command mode, and emacs
     mode.  The default is vi insert mode.  The program can switch the default
     to emacs mode by using the el_set(3) or el_parse(3) functions, and the
     user can switch to emacs mode either in the editrc(5) configuration file
     or interactively with the eedd--ccoommmmaanndd editor command, in all three cases
     executing the bbiinndd --ee builtin command.

     If trying to read from the terminal results in end of file or an error,
     the library signals end of file to the program and does not return a
     string.

